  "worked_solution": "Recall that \n\n- ${max}_{x\\in S}f(x)$ is the maximum output value, while\n\n- $\\operatorname{arg}⁡{max}_{x\\in S}f(x)$ is an input in $S$ where that maximum output occurs.\n\nOn the other hand,\n\n- ${min}_{x\\in S}f(x)$ is the minimum output value, while\n\n- $\\operatorname{arg}⁡{min}_{x\\in S}f(x)$ is an input in $S$ where that minimum output occurs.\n\nThe output values are $-2,1,-1,$ and $5.$ The maximum output is $5$ (at $t=3$), and the minimum output is $-2$ (at $t=-4$). \n\nTherefore, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{max}_{t\\in T}g(t) & =5 \\\\ \\operatorname{arg}⁡{max}_{t\\in T}g(t) & =3 \\\\ {min}_{t\\in T}g(t) & =-2 \\\\ \\operatorname{arg}⁡{min}_{t\\in T}g(t) & =-4\\end{aligned}\n$$",
